# a layout that many members name is asked once whether its slots prove plans. Thirty levels of records, six members a level, all six of the next level's type: asked once for each member that names it, the lowest layout would be asked 6^30 times, and this file would never end
# nothing but a number leaves the program, so Link knows every writer of every field, and the texts are written by type as they are for one level
# f1 = few, f2 = sendList, f3 = sendBox, f4 = shape
